// Train-de-vie evaluation section (R. 553-3 to R. 553-3-7): scope,
// ten-item scale, reference-period renvoi, private-use prorata,
// adversarial procedure, disproportion threshold, exceptional
// circumstances, reporting chain.
//
// R. 553-3-2 (reference period = R. 532-1 / R. 543-5 mechanics) is a
// pure renvoi to the income-PF and ARS lines: no rule, SOURCE_ONLY
// (reason journaled). R. 553-3-3 (private-use prorata, professional
// exclusion) is implemented through the part_privee slots of the
// R. 553-3-1 rules, which cite both articles.
//
// DEONTIC MAP: the section is computational (institutional statuses)
// with three organ duties (inform the allocataire by registered letter
// with acknowledgement of receipt and the full 1/2 content R. 553-3-4,
// notify a motivated refusal by registered letter with AR R. 553-3-6,
// report up the chain R. 553-3-7) and one organ judgment
// ("circonstances exceptionnelles", section 47.3). R. 553-3-6 keeps
// grant two ways: exceptional circumstances (judgment) or established
// cessation of the marked disproportion (stated fact). The R. 553-3-7
// local report is conforming only when transmitted without delay
// (stated, no fixed calendar in the source), anonymised, and carrying
// the four particulars: reply timeliness 1°, decision direction 2°,
// evaluated items 3° (attested: no list type), sanction kind/amount
// 4° (or its stated absence); the national bilan must carry those
// elements over to the minister.
// The regulatory disproportion test (R. 553-3-5) is distinct from the
// L. 553-5 organ finding (07): it feeds it as evidence, channels stay
// separate (DECISION-0194).
// Rate map (R. 553-3-1, PC-A11): 1-2 rental value in full (no rate),
// 3/4/6/8/9 at 80 %, 5 at 25 % of market value over 10 000 EUR,
// 7 at 3 %, 10 at 10 % of capital.
//
// INPUT CONTRACTS (PC-R05-03/04/05: per-item, per-category gating):
// - 1°/2° rental values are per Bien (batie/non_batie_bien_valeur +
//   inapplicable flag per item); direct or occupied-dwelling fallback
//   (same dwelling amount per fallback item) is retained per item, and
//   each item contributes its apport (100 %, prorata). Mixed
//   direct+fallback across items sums both; no whole-category fallback
//   suppresses another direct property.
// - 3°/4°/6°/8°/9° spending aggregates cover every listed subcategory
//   (3 travaux+charges+entretien, 4 personnels+services, 6 menager+
//   hifi-video+informatique, 8 voyages+hotels+locations+restaurants+
//   reception+culturels+educatifs+communication+loisirs, 9 clubs+
//   chasse); the caller sums subcategories upstream. Each spending
//   apport requires household benefit during the reference period
//   (II 1°, depenses_foyer_periode_reference); categories without
//   spending derive no apport and do not block the total.
// - 5°/7° market values are per Bien with per-item disposal date
//   (II 2°) and per-item value-bearing evidence (assurance amount,
//   professional-estimate amount, publication reference value, each
//   Money per Bien when available, or explicit sans_preuve); the
//   assessed real value plus its date plus one available evidence
//   (or attested absence) yields the institutional retained value
//   per Bien, and each item derives its apport only from that
//   retained value. No equality with an evidence amount, no evidence
//   hierarchy, no averaging: differing insurance/retained amounts are
//   lawful where the assessment accounts for the evidence. 5° tests
//   >10 000 EUR per vehicle ("de chaque bien"), 25 %; 7° is 3 %;
//   <=10k vehicles and missing dates/evidence yield no apport
//   (not zero).
// - The total is the sum of all derived apports (no blanket dates or
//   period); it requires the complete inventory
//   (inventaire_tdv_complet) and the section. Capital (10°) needs no
//   period; property needs no dates.
// - The plafond comes from the benefit packages; excluded incomes
//   (R. 532-3..8) arrive as provenanced facts.

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package fr.pf.core version "0.1.0";
